CardioFlow
Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Benjamin Ta

This repository holds material under more than one set of terms. The source
code and the bundled anatomical meshes did not come from the same place and
cannot be covered by one licence, so each is stated separately below.

Nothing here is a medical device. CardioFlow is an educational simulation built
on simplified physiological models, and no licence granted below should be read
as a warranty that any output is clinically valid.


================================================================================
1. THE SOURCE CODE
================================================================================

All rights reserved.

This covers everything written for this project: the physiology engine under
packages/engine, the web application under apps/web, the reference service
under services/api, the asset build scripts under tools/, and the test suites.

No open-source licence has been chosen for it yet. Until one is, the code is
under ordinary copyright and carries no grant of use, copying, modification or
redistribution beyond what applicable law allows without permission.

The physiological models the code implements are published science and are not
claimed here. Each one is cited at the point it is used and again in the
assumption register at packages/engine/src/models/assumptions.ts, which names
the paper every constant and every curve came from. Luo and Rudy's ionic model,
Dower's transform, Severinghaus's dissociation curve, Murray's law and the rest
belong to their authors. What is covered above is this implementation of them.


================================================================================
2. THE ANATOMICAL MESHES  (apps/web/public/anatomy/)
================================================================================

These files are adapted from two external datasets and remain under those
datasets' licences. Section 1 does not apply to them.


2a. BodyParts3D  --  CC Attribution-Share Alike 2.1 Japan
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Covers: cardiovascular.glb, cerebral.glb, and every organ and vessel mesh
within them.

    BodyParts3D, (c) The Database Center for Life Science, licensed under
    CC Attribution-Share Alike 2.1 Japan.

    Source:  https://dbarchive.biosciencedbc.jp/data/bodyparts3d/LATEST
    Licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.1/jp/deed.en

The .glb bundles in this repository are adapted material. They were decimated,
welded, Draco-compressed and transformed into the simulator's coordinate frame
by tools/anatomy/build.mjs, which records the download URL, the simplification
targets and the transform so that the result can be reproduced rather than
taken on trust.

SHARE-ALIKE: because they are adapted material, those bundles are distributed
under the same CC BY-SA 2.1 Japan licence as the originals. Anyone
redistributing them, or any further adaptation of them, must do the same and
must carry the attribution above. This obligation attaches to the meshes alone.
It does not reach the source code, which is a separate work that loads them.

The attribution is also shown in the running application, as required by a
licence that asks for credit reasonable to the medium: in full on the About
page, and compactly on every scene that draws the meshes.


2b. HuBMAP CCF 3D Reference Object Library  --  CC BY 4.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Covers: surface-female.glb, surface-male.glb, lung-female.glb, lung-male.glb.

    Kristen Browne, Heidi Schlehlein, Bruce W. Herr II, Ellen Quardokus,
    Andreas Bueckle, Katy Borner. 2024. HuBMAP CCF 3D Reference Object
    Library. humanatlas.io/3d-reference-library. Licensed CC BY 4.0.

    Source:  https://humanatlas.io/3d-reference-library
    Licence: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Attribution only, with no share-alike obligation. A second source was needed
because BodyParts3D contains exactly one body, an adult male, so drawing every
subject with it would have shown half of them the wrong body. It also has no
lung parenchyma at all, filing only the bronchi and pulmonary vessels under
that name.


================================================================================
3. THE DRACO DECODER  (apps/web/public/draco/)
================================================================================

draco_decoder.js, draco_decoder.wasm and draco_wasm_wrapper.js are Google's
Draco mesh decoder, redistributed unmodified so that the browser can read the
compressed meshes without fetching them from a third-party CDN.

    Copyright The Draco Authors
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
    Source: https://github.com/google/draco

Section 1 does not apply to them.


